I was hanging out with the cool kids in rec.games.roguelike.nethack when 
azgor got out a spraycan and scrawled the following:
>  [8]: Tourists #chatting with monsters can get directions
>  (clairvoyance). Need to find a way of giving POOR directions from
>  chaotic monsters though... --mathx

There was a scrolling, get-out-of-the-dungeon-style adventure game I
played on an 8-bit computer of some description, in which you could stop
and talk to prisoners and be given directions.  These directions were
presented in the form of the path to the exit being lit up for a short
period.

I can't remember any more about it, and so the YANI is maddeningly
vague, but I really like this one, to the extent that I don't think it
should be restricted to tourists.  I might have to think about it some
more.

>  [17]: If your luck is in the negative, rooms are generated dark far
>  more often. --Patashu
>  
